                <pb facs="1170" n="1156" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/9–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-01T22:00:00-04:00">September 1,
                            1944—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1163. 1. Please refer to Articles II and III of the Treaty for the Relinquishment
                    of Extraterritorial Rights in China, signed on January 11, 1943.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d872-f1"/> These Articles provide that the Chinese Government, in
                    taking over administration and control of the Diplomatic Quarter at Peiping and
                    the International Settlements at Shanghai and Amoy, will make provision for the
                    assumption and discharge of the official obligations and liabilities of the
                    Diplomatic Quarter and of those Settlements and for the recognition and
                    protection of all legitimate rights therein.</p>
                <p>2. Department feels that the satisfactory implementation of these provisions is
                    important and would like to know what measures the Chinese Government has
                    already taken or contemplates taking to carry out its undertaking. Please
                    informally discuss this matter with Dr. Soong<anchor n="2" xml:id="d872-f2"/> at
                    an early date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
